{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"izar","id":"566079740591603714","is_bot":0,"username":"izarsystem"},"author_id":"566079740591603714","channel_id":"736445407357304852","content":"||Cato.  \n\nFrom the moment I met you,\nOn that roof in London, watching the stars, \nGazing at the celestial craters of a moon reflected in our dreams, \nYour love was there.  I knew that instant you were special. \nYou looked up at the stars with me and I showed you my passions. \n\nI saw the awe and the wisdom in your beautiful eyes and you looked at me in a way nobody’d ever seen me before.\n\n  When I saw we’d be sharing a room, every cell within me screamed for you.  \nThat night, after I’d announced the ball. \nI’d done it hoping you’d ask me, and you did. \nYou asked if I could teach you how to dance. \nI took you down to the engine room, and we danced. \nWe danced to memories of a better future.  \n\nI asked you to marry me. \nAnd we planned. \nWe were going to have a big barbecue and a ball outside and we were going to be married.  \n\nWe talked about adopting Skitter. \nAnd sponsoring Wren. \nAnd adopting all the children who were lost.   \n\nBefore the fight. \nBefore that wretched, fated, horrible collection of moments,\nYou asked me to stay. \nI didn’t stay. \nI dragged us both into this. \nI thought I could be as wise and courageous as you were. I was wrong. I’m sorry. I failed you.  \n\nCato Zephyr, I love you with all my soul, and I pray one day our souls will return to each other’s embrace. You are my starlit sky, my sun-dappled forest, my love.||","created_at":"2020-07-30T07:17:34.689000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-30T07:18:01.703000Z","id":"738294202374291486","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
